  "reply_raw": "<think>**Evaluating database rules**\n\nI need to set a narrow standing rule for the production database tier 1, ensuring the time-to-live (TTL) is less than or equal to 30 for active purposes. The resources in the production database support minimal recurring tasks, about four. I could use a wildcard approach for broader tasks, but it might introduce risks by considering all resources in staging too. So, I’ll ensure the conditions around TTL are appropriate to support only one per attribute as long as it stays below that limit.</think>\n\n{\"mode\":\"precedent\",\"rule\":{\"action\":\"attach_role\",\"resource\":\"prod-db\",\"conditions\":{\"incident_active\":[\"eq\",\"1\"],\"scope_match\":[\"eq\",\"1\"],\"role_tier\":[\"eq\",\"1\"],\"ttl_min\":[\"le\",30],\"purpose\":[\"eq\",\"availability\"]}}}",
